                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "645cce6c-0f99-3bce-b6c5-d8fceed24045",
                        "entry_id": "b9f71b62-a9c1-3f0b-99fa-f8e4c2fb6925",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make (more) coarse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a413acd7-b61f-48c2-b789-507f25bc4d9b",
                                "sense_id": "645cce6c-0f99-3bce-b6c5-d8fceed24045",
                                "text": "1941, Emily Carr, Klee Wyck, Chapter 6 \"D'Sonoqua,\" http://www.gutenberg.net.au/ebooks01/0100131h.html\nShe appeared to be neither wooden nor stationary, but a singing spirit, young and fresh, passing through the jungle. No violence coarsened her; no power domineered to wither her. She was graciously feminine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "df963437-8c3f-44c3-b03c-82abdb91c072",
                                "sense_id": "645cce6c-0f99-3bce-b6c5-d8fceed24045",
                                "text": "[…] as the years went by, democracy and its wide audiences tended to broaden and coarsen humor."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2cd5a9a3-0e22-481e-8189-fdabadd3d81b",
                                "sense_id": "645cce6c-0f99-3bce-b6c5-d8fceed24045",
                                "text": "Because the wool is of poor quality, it will coarsen the fabric."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4357f7fb-3c6d-3787-b118-7e80a9c80d1a",
                        "entry_id": "b9f71b62-a9c1-3f0b-99fa-f8e4c2fb6925",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To become (more) coarse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "030d51ff-ec95-4825-8f0d-e647fb48f31b",
                                "sense_id": "4357f7fb-3c6d-3787-b118-7e80a9c80d1a",
                                "text": "He was intolerable now except under the influence of liquor, and as he seemed to decay and coarsen under her eyes, Gloria's soul and body shrank away from him […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c696ee0a-008a-48c0-8d22-d568986a5d24",
                                "sense_id": "4357f7fb-3c6d-3787-b118-7e80a9c80d1a",
                                "text": "[…] though her skin had coarsened in the last ten years, the dark red of her cheeks and lips was as vivid as ever."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
